ute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"id"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether this element is at the top or the bottom of the bracket.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"kind"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Distinguishes multiple non-arpeggiate elements on a single note.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"number"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"placement"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNonArpeggiate":{"title":"MXLNonArpeggiate","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnonarpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The non-arpeggiate type indicates that this note is at the top or bottom of a bracket indicating to not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate these notes. Since this does not involve playback, it is only used on the top or bottom notes, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on each note as for the arpeggiate type."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNonArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNonArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonArpeggiate"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTopBottom":{"abstract":[{"text":"The top-bottom type is used to indicate the top or bottom part of a vertical shape like non-arpeggiate